    "body": "The way JS solved this was `type=module` on `<script>` and a corresponding `nomodule` attribute for fallbacks etc, which also allows fallbacks that are *different* (in JS that was essential since the syntax is incompatible, but I can see it being useful here too). I don't think this pattern was considered, at least last time I looked at the doc.",
