    "updated_at": "2026-10-09T04:48:27Z",
    "body": "I agree with @noamr about `modulepreload`. But also, an `import` attribute isn't consistent with that either, `modulepreload` still uses `href`. \n\nSo it's about following one of two existing precedents vs creating a third 😅\n\nFWIW I do think `import` _might_ be a better design — I kinda wish `<script>` and `modulepreload` had gone that way as well. But given that they didn't, I don't think it passes the bar of being so much better as to warrant [breaking consistency](https://www.w3.org/TR/design-principles/#consistency) and introducing a third pattern. \n\nThat said, neither `<script src>` nor `<link rel=modulepreload href>` actually accept specifiers, only URLs, so perhaps that's the distinction that justifies an `import` attribute (and then we could also add it to the other two). ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
