    "body": "\r\n> That said, neither `<script src>` nor `<link rel=modulepreload href>` actually accept specifiers, only URLs, so perhaps that's the distinction that justifies an `import` attribute (and then we could also add it to the other two).\r\n\r\nAlso `<script type=module>` works without `src`, so it doesn't necessarily import.\r\nBut yes - that's the more important distinction... making `href` support something that's not a document-relative URL based on the `type` attribute is a bit awkward.",
