    "body": "I don't know if `type=\"module\"`/`nomodule` pattern is a good fit for `<link>`:\r\n\r\n* Semantics of `type` on `<link>`: On `<script>`, type was overloaded for \"module\" and \"importmap\" because <script> has no rel attribute. On <link>, rel defines the processing model while type is just an advisory MIME type hint (which is also why we have `rel=\"modulepreload\"` rather than `rel=\"preload\" type=\"module\"`).\r\n* Simpler fallback without `nomodule`: Because module stylesheets may use bare specifiers, using `href` with `type=\"module\"` requires authoring two separate `<link>` elements with `nomodule` for fallback. With the proposed `import` attribute, a single `<link rel=\"stylesheet\" import=\"foo\" href=\"fallback.css\">` gracefully falls back to `href` in legacy browsers without needing `nomodule` at all.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/6076469916/reactions",
