    "body": "> That said, neither <script src> nor <link rel=modulepreload href> actually accept specifiers, only URLs, so perhaps that's the distinction that justifies an import attribute (and then we could also add it to the other two).\r\n\r\n@LeaVerou - yeah, the extensibility aspect on other elements is pretty great for `import`. Another other nice thing is that we could use `export` [for declarative inline modules](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11687) instead of `specifier` and there would be some nice symmetry.",
