    "body": "Is FOUC addressed by this? If not, it seems very unlikely to be used in declarative Shadow DOM. It's likely also not acceptable unless explicitly specified.\r\n\r\nI believe currently, blocking rendering only happens if the link is potentially render-blocking, and a document stops accepting render-blocking elements once `<body>` exists. So a `<link import>` inside a declarative shadow root in `<body>` never blocks rendering. Even when the specifier is already in the module map, setting the link’s sheet is queued as a task. So every instance after the first can paint unstyled.",
